// The Windows application icon.
//
// Everything Windows draws for this program outside its own window - the
// taskbar button, the Explorer file icon, the Start menu and desktop
// shortcuts, the Alt+Tab card - comes from an icon RESOURCE compiled into the
// executable. Not from setWindowIcon, which only reaches the window itself,
// and not from the installer, which points its shortcuts at the exe and takes
// whatever icon the exe carries. There was no resource, so all of it was the
// generic Windows placeholder while a perfectly good icon sat in the repo.
//
// IDI_ICON1 is the conventional name for it: Windows shows the icon resource
// with the lowest name, and the shell looks for this one first.
//
// The .ico carries 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128 and 256 pixel images. All of them
// matter - the taskbar takes 32, the Alt+Tab card 48 or 256 depending on the
// display, and a scaled-down 256 into a 16 px slot is a smear.
IDI_ICON1 ICON "../assets/branding/graphvis.ico"
